Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:41:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] macOS: stand-ins for the Linux-only headers NEO includes

shared/source/os_interface/macos/include is put before the system
headers on macOS. Each file is the least the Linux DRM backend and
sysman need to compile; none of them fakes a kernel interface:
linux/types.h, linux/limits.h, linux/const.h, linux/bits.h (the DRM uAPI
headers), sys/prctl.h (PR_SET_PTRACER; SysCalls::prctl fails with
ENOSYS), sys/sysmacros.h, sys/sysinfo.h (get_nprocs_conf), link.h
(struct link_map and RTLD_DI_LINKMAP for SysCalls::dlinfo),
linux/perf_event.h and mtd/mtd-user.h (sysman: no event source and no
MTD node exist, so nothing is ever opened), and sys/socket.h with an
emulated SOCK_CLOEXEC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
